  "projectUrl": "https://github.com/georgepwall1991/CancelCop.Analyzer",
  "published": "2026-07-27T00:51:15.707Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "CC028 now covers the System.IO.Stream primitives — Read, Write, CopyTo, and Flush — closing a silent false negative: the rule previously keyed on the exact declaring type name (File, StreamReader, StreamWriter), so blocking stream calls in async code were never flagged despite each having a token-taking async counterpart. Stream types match by inheritance, so FileStream, NetworkStream, GZipStream, and user-defined subclasses are covered; MemoryStream is excluded as in-memory. The suggested rewrite is validated against the overload the call would actually bind to, so it always compiles. Diagnostic IDs and severities are unchanged from 1.28.1.",
